;;; An hrule's `:assert (not ?g)` with `?g` bound to a guest puts `(not Ann)` in H —
;;; M1f **W84**, register row `W84/not-name-hrule-concluded`, filed by S1f.7.4 (T1f.7.4.2,
;;; 2026-11-11).
;;;
;;; ── What this program is ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; Two guests, of whom Ann has paid, and an hrule that proposes `(not ?g)` of whoever
;;; has paid.
;;;
;;; ── The answer, by hand ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; `(not Ann)` is the negation of no fact, so it is no hypothesis: refused at load,
;;; one line, on every command. Without the hrule's candidate H is empty and R is
;;; {∅}.
;;;
;;; ── What the engine answered ──────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; At `55aadd0b`, release: the program loads; H is the one candidate `(not Ann)`, and R is
;;; two states, ∅ and {(not Ann)}, which differ in a fact nothing can read: the goal
;;; answers `?g = Ann` in both, exit 0 on every command.
;;; Refused at load since S1f.7.4 (T1f.7.4.3).

(relation paid Guest :why "{?1} has paid")
(is-a Ann Guest) (is-a Bob Guest)
(paid Ann)
(hrule suppose () :match (paid ?g) :assert (not ?g) :why "suppose not {?g}")
(query :goal (paid ?g))
